          \"summary\":<insight_1_summary>,\n                \"explanation\": <insight_1_explanation>\n            }},\n            {{\n                \"summary\":<insight_2_summary>,\n                \"explanation\": <insight_2_explanation>\n            }}\n        ]\n    }}\n\n# Grounding Rules\n\nPoints supported by data should list their data references as follows:\n\n\"This is an example sentence supported by multiple data references [Data: <dataset name> (record ids); <dataset name> (record ids)].\"\n\nDo not list more than 5 record ids in a single reference. Instead, list the top 5 most relevant record ids and add \"+more\" to indicate that there are more.\n\nFor example:\n\"Person X is the owner of Company Y and subject to many allegations of wrongdoing [Data: Reports (1), Entities (5, 7); Relationships (23); Claims (7, 2, 34, 64, 46, +more)].\"\n\nwhere 1, 5, 7, 23, 2, 34, 46, and 64 represent the id (not the index) of the relevant data record.\n\nDo not include information where the supporting evidence for it is not provided.\n\n\n# Example Input\n-----------\nText:\n\nEntities\n\nid,entity,description\n5,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n6,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is an organization that is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n\nRelationships\n\nid,source,target,description\n37,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,Verdant Oasis Plaza is the location of the Unity March\n38,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,Harmony Assembly is holding a march at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n39,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,UNITY MARCH,The Unity March is taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n40,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,TRIBUNE SPOTLIGHT,Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity march taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza\n41,VERDANT OASIS PLAZA,BAILEY ASADI,Bailey Asadi is speaking at Verdant Oasis Plaza about the march\n43,HARMONY ASSEMBLY,UNITY MARCH,Harmony Assembly is organizing the Unity March\n\nOutput:\n{{\n    \"title\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza and Unity March\",\n    \"summary\": \"The community revolves around the Verdant Oasis Plaza, which is the location of the Unity March. The plaza has relationships with the Harmony Assembly, Unity March, and Tribune Spotlight, all of which are associated with the march event.\",\n    \"rating\": 5.0,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is moderate due to the potential for unrest or conflict during the Unity March.\",\n    \"findings\": [\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza as the central location\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Verdant Oasis Plaza is the central entity in this community, serving as the location for the Unity March. This plaza is the common link between all other entities, suggesting its significance in the community. The plaza's association with the march could potentially lead to issues such as public disorder or conflict, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. [Data: Entities (5), Relationships (37, 38, 39, 40, 41,+more)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Harmony Assembly's role in the community\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Harmony Assembly is another key entity in this community, being the organizer of the march at Verdant Oasis Plaza. The nature of Harmony Assembly and its march could be a potential source of threat, depending on their objectives and the reactions they provoke. The relationship between Harmony Assembly and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Entities(6), Relationships (38, 43)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Unity March as a significant event\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Unity March is a significant event taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza. This event is a key factor in the community's dynamics and could be a potential source of threat, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. The relationship between the march and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Relationships (39)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Role of Tribune Spotlight\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity March taking place in Verdant Oasis Plaza. This suggests that the event has attracted media attention, which could amplify its impact on the community. The role of Tribune Spotlight could be significant in shaping public perception of the event and the entities involved. [Data: Relationships (40)]\"\n        }}\n    ]\n}}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n----Reports-----\ncommunity,full_content\r\n1153,\"# Chronic and Acute Kidney Insufficiency Community\n\nThis community encompasses various entities related to chronic and acute kidney insufficiency, including conditions, treatments, and nutritional management strategies. The interconnectedness of these entities highlights the complexity of managing kidney-related health issues and the critical role of nutrition in treatment outcomes.\n\n## Chronic Kidney Failure as a Major Health Concern\n\nChronic kidney failure (INSUFICIENCIA RENAL CRÓNICA) is a long-term condition that leads to the gradual loss of kidney function, significantly impacting patients' health and quality of life. This condition is often associated with complications such as malnutrition, cardiovascular risks, and the need for interventions like dialysis or transplantation. The management of chronic kidney failure requires a multifaceted approach, including dietary restrictions and careful monitoring of nutritional intake to mitigate associated risks. [Data: Entities (2193); Relationships (5668, 7272, 7705, 8399, 9165, +more)]\n\n## Acute Kidney Failure and Its Immediate Risks\n\nAcute renal failure (INSUFICIENCIA RENAL AGUDA) is characterized by a sudden loss of kidney function, which can be reversible or irreversible. This condition often arises as a complication of other medical issues, necessitating immediate medical intervention and tailored nutritional management. Patients with acute renal failure face specific dietary needs to support recovery and prevent further complications, highlighting the importance of timely and effective treatment strategies. [Data: Entities (2183); Relationships (4756, 2716, 9120, 9121, 9123, +more)]\n\n## The Role of Dialysis in Kidney Management\n\nDialysis, including both hemodialysis (HEMODIÁLISIS) and peritoneal dialysis (DIÁLISIS PERITONEAL), is a critical treatment for patients with kidney failure. These procedures are essential for removing waste products and excess fluids from the blood when the kidneys are unable to perform these functions. Dialysis not only addresses immediate health needs but also requires careful dietary management to ensure patients receive adequate nutrition while undergoing treatment. [Data: Entities (2200, 2185, 2191); Relationships (9141, 9121, 9123, 9127, 9142, +more)]\n\n## Nutritional Management as a Key Component\n\nNutritional management is vital for patients with both chronic and acute kidney insufficiency. Specific dietary guidelines, such as low-protein diets, are recommended to manage the condition effectively and prevent malnutrition. Nutritional support strategies are essential for maintaining health and improving the quality of life for these patients, emphasizing the interconnectedness of nutrition and kidney health. [Data: Entities (10094, 10082); Relationships (2638, 2716, 756, 755, 9164, +more)]\n\n## Complications Associated with Kidney Insufficiency\n\nPatients with kidney insufficiency often face various complications, including hyperkalemia, malnutrition, and secondary hyperparathyroidism. These conditions arise due to the kidneys' inability to maintain electrolyte balance and nutrient absorption, necessitating comprehensive management strategies to address these issues. Understanding these complications is crucial for healthcare providers to develop effective treatment plans for affected individuals. [Data: Entities (11382, 10068, 5616); Relationships (9165, 9160, 9159, 7278, 7279, +more)]\"\r\n1154,\"# Nutritional Management in Renal and Respiratory Insufficiency\n\nThis community focuses on the interrelated medical conditions of renal insufficiency and respiratory failure, emphasizing the critical role of specialized nutritional support. Key entities include various forms of nutritional interventions and guidelines that are essential for managing these health issues, highlighting the complex interplay between nutrition and these conditions.\n\n## Critical role of nutritional support in renal insufficiency\n\nNutritional support is vital for patients with renal insufficiency, as their ability to filter waste is compromised, leading to various health complications. Specialized nutritional interventions, such as parenteral and enteral nutrition, are often required to meet the unique dietary needs of these patients. For instance, parenteral nutrition becomes essential when the gastrointestinal tract is not functional, ensuring that patients receive necessary nutrients and fluids while managing their altered physiological needs [Data: Relationships (4635, 2610, 712, 6754, 6856)].\n\n## Impact of comorbidities on renal insufficiency management\n\nConditions such as diabetes and obesity significantly complicate the management of renal insufficiency. These comorbidities can exacerbate the challenges faced by patients, making tailored nutritional strategies even more critical. For example, diabetes can lead to further renal damage, while obesity increases the risk of renal insufficiency due to metabolic changes, necessitating careful dietary planning to mitigate these risks [Data: Relationships (5792, 5904, 6850)].\n\n## Guidelines provided by ASPEN 7\n\nASPEN 7 offers comprehensive guidelines for nutritional management in patients with renal insufficiency and respiratory failure. These guidelines are crucial for healthcare providers to ensure that patients receive appropriate nutritional support tailored to their specific conditions. The recommendations include strategies for managing fluid and electrolyte balance, which are particularly important for patients undergoing treatments like hemodialysis [Data: Entities (12910), Relationships (6870, 6848)].\n\n## Consequences of malnutrition in renal patients\n\nMalnutrition, particularly caloric-protein malnutrition, is a common consequence of renal insufficiency. This condition can lead to severe health deterioration, making it imperative to implement effective nutritional strategies. The interplay between renal function and nutritional status is critical, as inadequate nutrient intake can further compromise kidney health and overall well-being [Data: Entities (10104, 15982), Relationships (6855, 6856)].\n\n## The significance of multidisciplinary teams\n\nMultidisciplinary teams play a crucial role in managing patients with renal insufficiency by designing tailored dietary plans that address the complex needs of these individuals. These teams often include dietitians, nephrologists, and other healthcare professionals who collaborate to optimize nutritional support and improve patient outcomes. Their collective expertise is essential in navigating the challenges posed by renal insufficiency and ensuring comprehensive care [Data: Relationships (5504)].\"\r\n1155,\"# Nutritional Assessment Community: Albumina and Related Proteins\n\nThe community focuses on the assessment of nutritional status through various proteins, primarily Albumina and Prealbumina, which are critical markers in clinical settings. These entities are interconnected through their roles in evaluating nutritional health, particularly in patients with chronic conditions, and are supported by various studies and indices.\n\n## Albumina as a key nutritional marker\n\nAlbumina is a vital protein that serves as a significant marker for assessing nutritional status and liver function in patients. Its levels are closely monitored in various clinical settings, particularly for patients undergoing surgery, those with cancer, and individuals with chronic kidney disease. Low levels of albumina can indicate compromised nutritional status, while increases may reflect improvements in nutritional intake, especially in patients receiving enteral nutrition. This protein's importance is underscored by its role in maintaining oncotic pressure and facilitating the transport of substances in the bloodstream [Data: Entities (1730); Relationships (3276, 648, 7409, 7394, 7405, +more)].\n\n## Prealbumina's role in nutritional evaluation\n\nPrealbumina is another crucial protein used to evaluate nutritional status, particularly in patients at risk of malnutrition. Its levels can provide insights into a patient's nutritional condition throughout treatment, making it a valuable prognostic marker. Prealbumina is especially significant in assessing patients with inflammatory bowel disease, where it reflects their nutritional status. The relationship between prealbumina and albumina highlights the interconnectedness of these proteins in nutritional assessments [Data: Entities (1732); Relationships (3277, 6982, 7419, 7330, 7418, +more)].\n\n## The Maastricht Index as a comprehensive assessment tool\n\nThe Maastricht Index is a prognostic index that utilizes various nutritional risk markers, including albumina and prealbumina, to assess nutritional status. This index is particularly useful in clinical settings for identifying patients at risk of malnutrition. Its application in evaluating nutritional health underscores the importance of these proteins in comprehensive assessments, especially in populations experiencing undernutrition [Data: Entities (4801); Relationships (710, 948, 7395, 7418, 14063, +more)].\n\n## BIA Multifrequency's contribution to body composition analysis\n\nMultifrequency bioelectrical impedance analysis (BIA) is a method used to estimate body water and composition, which is particularly useful in clinical settings. This technique can help monitor changes in body composition related to conditions such as sarcopenia and edematous states. The integration of BIA with nutritional assessments enhances the understanding of a patient's overall health and nutritional status, making it a valuable tool in managing chronic conditions [Data: Entities (4802); Relationships (1690, 14066, 14064, +more)].\n\n## DOPPS study's insights into dialysis patients\n\nThe Dialysis Outcomes and Practice Patterns Study (DOPPS) evaluates the outcomes of dialysis patients, including their nutritional status across various demographics. This study confirms the prognostic value of albumina levels in assessing the risk of mortality in dialysis patients, highlighting the critical role of nutritional markers in managing chronic kidney disease. The findings from DOPPS contribute significantly to understanding the relationship between nutritional health and patient outcomes in this vulnerable population [Data: Entities (10075); Relationships (7399, 18149, 18148, +more)].\"\r\n\n\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n1897,COMPLICACIONES,\"\"\"COMPLICACIONES\"\" refers to the potential adverse effects and issues that can arise from various medical treatments and conditions. These complications can manifest in several contexts, including the use of feeding tubes, surgical procedures for obesity treatment, and the management of chronic conditions such as diabetes.\n\nIn the context of enteral nutrition, complications may include mechanical, gastrointestinal, and metabolic problems, particularly affecting pediatric patients. Specific adverse effects associated with enteral nutrition can involve increased gastric residue and diarrhea. Additionally, complications can arise from parenteral nutrition, such as thrombophlebitis and issues related to an excess of macronutrients.\n\nSurgical procedures, especially those related to obesity treatment, carry their own set of risks, including complications that must be prevented and managed during the postoperative period. Patients with cancer may also experience adverse effects during or after surgical interventions. Furthermore, complications may arise from inadequate nutrition in critically ill patients, necessitating nutritional interventions to address these health issues.\n\nOverall, \"\"COMPLICACIONES\"\" encompasses a wide range of potential health issues that can arise during treatment, highlighting the importance of monitoring and addressing these risks to ensure patient safety and effective care.\",19\r\n2154,ESTANCIA HOSPITALARIA,\"\"\"ESTANCIA HOSPITALARIA\"\" refers to the duration of time a patient spends in the hospital. This period is significant as it can be influenced by various factors, including nutritional status, complications arising during surgery, and specific medical conditions such as hyponatremia. Efforts are often made to reduce the length of hospital stay through appropriate nutritional interventions, such as enteral nutrition, which is designed to be immunomodulatory. The goal of these nutritional strategies is to enhance patient recovery and minimize the time spent in the hospital, thereby improving overall health outcomes.\",7\r\n4225,ENFERMEDAD RENAL CRÓNICA,\"Chronic kidney disease (enfermedad renal crónica, ERC) is a long-term medical condition characterized by the kidneys' inability to function effectively, often associated with diabetes. It is defined by a glomerular filtration rate (GFR) below 60 ml/min for at least three months, which can lead to various health complications. The disease is classified into different stages, with stage 3 considered to be of high cardiovascular risk, and stages 4-5 or those requiring dialysis classified as very high risk.\n\nManagement of chronic kidney disease necessitates dietary restrictions and specialized nutritional formulas, particularly in advanced stages. It requires careful monitoring of phosphorus intake to prevent further complications. Additionally, chronic kidney disease can invalidate the results of catecholamine and metanephrine tests used in diagnosing pheochromocytoma. The condition also complicates the management of acute diarrhea, necessitating special attention in treatment. Overall, chronic kidney disease is a serious condition that demands comprehensive medical and nutritional care.\",14\r\n939,FIGURA 5,\"FIGURA 5 encompasses a variety of illustrations and representations related to clinical nutrition and food preparation. It includes an illustration of a chinois or food mill, which is utilized for food preparation in various recipes. Additionally, FIGURA 5 depicts the variation of protein solubility as a function of pH in clinical nutrition products, providing insights into the biochemical aspects of nutrition. Furthermore, it illustrates a strategy for diagnosing malnutrition, detailing the essential steps involved in nutritional risk screening and assessment. Lastly, FIGURA 5 presents a specially designed cup intended for patients with swallowing difficulties, which aims to enhance safety during hydration. Overall, FIGURA 5 serves as a comprehensive resource that integrates food preparation tools, nutritional science, and patient care strategies.\",3\r\n11475,HOSPITALIZADOS,\"The term \"\"HOSPITALIZADOS\"\" refers to hospitalized patients, who are individuals receiving medical care in a hospital setting. These patients often require nutritional support during their stay to aid in their recovery and overall health management.\",2\r\n8070,ALIANZA MÁSNUTRIDOS,\"Alianza Másnutridos is a coalition in Spain dedicated to tackling malnutrition associated with disease through a multidisciplinary approach. The organization focuses on implementing screening processes at various levels of healthcare to identify and address malnutrition effectively. Additionally, Alianza Másnutridos aims to raise awareness and integrate the issue of malnutrition into national and regional health strategies, ensuring that it is recognized as a critical component of public health initiatives.\",17\r\n8071,SOCIEDAD ESPAÑOLA DE NUTRICIÓN ENTERAL Y PARENTERAL,\"The \"\"Sociedad Española de Nutrición Enteral y Parenteral\"\" (SENPE) is a professional organization dedicated to the promotion and development of enteral and parenteral nutrition in Spain. It focuses on providing resources and support for clinical nutrition, particularly for patients with specific needs such as renal insufficiency and those undergoing hemodialysis. SENPE publishes guidelines and studies that address various aspects of nutritional support, including the administration and absorption of medications in patients receiving enteral nutrition. Through its efforts, SENPE aims to enhance the quality of nutritional care and ensure that healthcare professionals have access to the latest information and best practices in the field of enteral and parenteral nutrition.\",6\r\n10066,PEW,\"Protein-energy wasting (PEW) is a syndrome characterized by the loss of body protein mass and energy reserves in chronic kidney disease patients, leading to malnutrition.\",2\r\n1911,HIPOFOSFATEMIA,\"Hipofosfatemia, also known as hypophosphatemia, is a medical condition defined by a serum phosphorus concentration below 2.5 mg/dl. This condition can occur in hospitalized patients and is often asymptomatic; however, it can lead to severe health issues if phosphorus levels drop below 1 mg/dl. Hypophosphatemia is characterized by low phosphate levels in the blood and can arise from various causes, including patients receiving parenteral nutrition. The condition is significant in clinical settings due to its potential complications and the need for appropriate management and treatment.\",6\r\n2498,ESCAPES DEL CONTENIDO GÁSTRICO,\"Gastric content leaks are complications that can occur around the catheter, leading to skin erosion and other issues.\",1\r\n2499,FUGAS A PERITONEO,Leaks into the peritoneum are serious complications that can arise from gastrostomy procedures.,1\r\n2500,FÍSTULAS GASTROCÓLICAS,\"Gastrocolic fistulas are abnormal connections that can develop between the stomach and colon, often as a complication of gastrostomy.\",1\r\n2501,DESCOLOCACIÓN INADVERTIDA DE LA SONDA,Inadvertent dislocation of the tube can lead to obstruction of the gastric outlet tract or displacement into the gastrocutaneous fistula tract.,1\r\n14875,EMERGENCIA,\"La inserción de catéteres venosos centrales en situaciones de emergencia puede aumentar el riesgo de complicaciones, incluyendo infecciones\",1\r\n8076,ALIANZA GENERAL DE PACIENTES,The Alianza General de Pacientes is an organization in Spain that represents patient interests and advocates for their rights in healthcare.,1\r\n8083,CONSEJO GENERAL DE COLEGIOS OFICIALES DE FARMACÉUTICOS,,1\r\n8075,CONSEJO GENERAL DE ENFERMERÍA,\"The Consejo General de Enfermería is the governing body for nursing professionals in Spain, promoting nursing standards and practices.\",1\r\n8077,SOCIEDAD ESPAÑOLA DE MEDICINA DE FAMILIA Y COMUNITARIA,The Sociedad Española de Medicina de Familia y Comunitaria (semFYC) is a professional society for family medicine practitioners in Spain.,1\r\n8078,SOCIEDAD ESPAÑOLA DE MÉDICOS DE ATENCIÓN PRIMARIA,The Sociedad Española de Médicos de Atención Primaria (SEMERGEN) is an organization focused on the interests and education of primary care physicians in Spain.,1\r\n8079,\"SOCIEDAD ESPAÑOLA DE GASTROENTEROLOGÍA, HEPATOLOGÍA Y NUTRICIÓN PEDIÁTRICA\",\"The Sociedad Española de Gastroenterología, Hepatología y Nutrición Pediátrica (SGHNP) is a professional society dedicated to pediatric gastroenterology and nutrition in Spain.\",1\r\n8084,SOCIEDAD ESPAÑOLA DE ONCOLOGÍA RADIOTERAPÉTICA,,1\r\n8081,FUNDACIÓN ABBOTT,\"Fundación Abbott is a foundation that supports health and nutrition initiatives, particularly